# clang-format 18 configuration for RocketNet's C and C++ style. Language Cpp
# covers .c and .h as well. It gives Allman braces, 4-space indent, spaces
# inside parentheses but not empty ones, `char * p`, `(T) value` casts, tight
# square brackets, unlimited line length, unsorted includes, indented case
# labels and namespaces, macro definition bodies left as written, and braces
# on every control statement body.
#
# The blank-line keys are set explicitly so that formatting never adds or
# removes a blank line a person placed (up to four in a row).
#
# What clang-format 18 cannot express, one per line; these are kept by hand:
#   trailing whitespace is kept on some lines; clang-format always strips it, no option keeps it
#   cast pointers bind to the type, `(sockaddr_in6*) p`; PointerAlignment sets casts and declarations together
#   sizeof is written tight, `sizeof(buffer)`; there is no sizeof-only parenthesis option
#   some calls and groupings are written tight; SpacesInParens has no per-call option
#   function-pointer declarators are tight, `void (*f)( ... )`; SpacesInParensOptions Other spaces declarator parentheses with call parentheses, no separate option
#   preprocessor lines are indented by hand, `    #if`; BeforeHash and AfterHash indent by depth everywhere; with IndentPPDirectives None they are pulled to column 0, so a preprocessor group indented by hand holds only inside a clang-format off region; sdk/rocketnet.h, whose groups are indented one level per #if with their doc comments (an include guard after #pragma once is not seen as a guard, so BeforeHash would also indent the whole header), sits between one clang-format off and on pair
#   preprocessor parentheses are tight, `#if defined(_WIN32)`, `#pragma warning(disable:4996)`; SpacesInParens has no preprocessor-only switch
#   short unions, enums and if/else blocks sit on one line, `union { ... } data;`; Allman wrapping splits them
#   byte tables keep several values per line; a braced list ending in a comma is broken one element per line, no option keeps it
#   `#if` conditions continue over backslash lines; with ColumnLimit 0 they are joined
#   case bodies and values sit at a hand-chosen column; short-case alignment pads to the longest label only
#   continuation arguments are sometimes indented one level, not aligned; AlignAfterOpenBracket has no per-call choice
#   declarations inside `#if` are indented; no option indents code by preprocessor depth; sdk/rocketnet.h indents the declarations and doc comments of its #if ROCKETNET_DEV block by hand, inside its off/on pair
#   spaces are hand-padded inside lines, `>> 8  )`, `x  = y`; there is no option for padding in expressions
#   binary operators inside an index are tight, `buffer[4*1024]`; binary operators are always spaced, no index-only option
#   some casts have no space after, `(uint32_t)INVALID_SOCKET`; SpaceAfterCStyleCast applies to every cast
#   tight binary operators in expressions, `(uint64_t(1)<<bits)`, and lines mixing several kinds above; no option keeps operators tight
#   macro parameter lists are hand-padded, `( stream, sequence, ack  )`; SkipMacroDefinitionBody skips the body only
#   comment-only lines inside a #define body are joined onto the line above, dropping their backslashes; SkipMacroDefinitionBody does not cover comments, so such macros sit between clang-format off and on
#   a #if or #elif condition continued over backslash lines is joined into one line (see above); these sit between clang-format off and on
#   a directive's trailing // comment followed by a // comment line gains a backslash that splices the two; that directive sits between clang-format off and on
#
# Braces, by the owner's ruling of 2026-11-10:
#   InsertBraces: true -- every if, else, for, while and do body is braced, "brackets are just safer". Braced by hand, because the formatter does not reach them: control statements inside a #define (SkipMacroDefinitionBody), a body that a preprocessor branch separates from its statement or that sits in a lambda holding a preprocessor branch (left unbraced), and a lambda body passed as a call argument (braces inserted but not placed)
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
BreakBeforeBraces: Allman
SpacesInParens: Custom
SpacesInParensOptions:
  InConditionalStatements: true
  InCStyleCasts: false
  InEmptyParentheses: false
  Other: true
SpacesInSquareBrackets: false
PointerAlignment: Middle
ReferenceAlignment: Middle
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: true
ColumnLimit: 0
SortIncludes: Never
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AlignConsecutiveShortCaseStatements:
  Enabled: true
  AcrossEmptyLines: false
  AcrossComments: false
  AlignCaseColons: false
AlignTrailingComments:
  Kind: Leave
IndentPPDirectives: None
IndentCaseLabels: true
IndentExternBlock: NoIndent
NamespaceIndentation: All
AccessModifierOffset: -4
EmptyLineAfterAccessModifier: Leave
AlwaysBreakTemplateDeclarations: No
Cpp11BracedListStyle: false
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 4
KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks: true
SeparateDefinitionBlocks: Leave
InsertBraces: true
RemoveBracesLLVM: false
FixNamespaceComments: false
ReflowComments: false
SkipMacroDefinitionBody: true
# declaration macros written tight in this style, `ROCKETNET_DECLARE_SENTINEL(0)`
WhitespaceSensitiveMacros:
  - ROCKETNET_DECLARE_SENTINEL
  - MAKEWORD
  - VERSION_STRING
